{
  "is_sufficient": false,
  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The gBCE implementation is underspecified: the report omits the exact correction, positive/negative loss normalization, and treatment of user-specific eligible catalog sizes and duplicate negatives. Excluding full training histories changes the sampling distribution.",
    "Negative sampling requires user identity or an aligned history-exclusion mask, but the diagnostic loader yields None rather than user IDs. The training sampler interface and fallback for fewer than 128 eligible items are unspecified.",
    "The literal pooling pseudocode recomputes pairwise similarities for every prefix, costing O(BL³d). A practical causal implementation, memory budget, decay parameterization, gate initialization, and padding behavior are missing; the difficulty rating of 4 is therefore optimistic.",
    "Because support lies between 0 and 1, its multiplicative contribution lies between 1 and 2. It may provide little recurrence discrimination while reinforcing popular-item similarity or suppressing legitimate minority interests. Compare against ordinary recency pooling and gBCE alone.",
    "The report lacks a budgeted experiment schedule, checkpoint-selection rule, and baseline validation HR@10. Its claimed potential and user alignment remain subjective; 20 simulator users cannot establish broad improvements in compatibility or purchase relevance."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Resolve the objective and sampling details needed for a faithful, numerically stable implementation.",
      "query": "In gSASRec's generalized binary cross-entropy paper and official implementation, what are the exact calibration exponent, sampling-rate definition, positive/negative loss normalization, and stable log-space formulation? How should these be interpreted when sampling 128 uniform negatives after excluding each user's observed training items, with possible duplicate negatives or fewer eligible items?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Determine whether the proposed residual can be implemented efficiently and whether recurrence weighting adds value beyond simple pooling.",
      "query": "For SASRec augmented with causal history pooling, how can support s_j(t)=mean over k<=t,k!=j of max(0,cos(e_j,e_k)) be computed for all prefixes using pairwise similarities and cumulative sums in O(BL²d), without future leakage? What sequential recommendation evidence compares similarity-weighted pooling with simple recency pooling and documents popularity amplification or loss of minority interests?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Ground the experiment design and prevent overstating gains from a small, repeatedly reused validation sample.",
      "query": "What do studies of sampled recommendation evaluation and adaptive validation selection imply for comparing SASRec, gBCE-only, recency-pooling-only, support-pooling-only, and combined models using fixed 99-negative HR@10 with 200 validation users per dataset? How should paired uncertainty, checkpoint selection, and a fixed GPU-time budget be handled without changing the evaluator or using test labels?"
    }
  ]
}
